            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery disease in Asian Indians.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>26-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary Heart Disease should new be considered an important public health problem in India. It is a part of the epidemiological transition characterized by changing lifestyles and a probable genetic predisposition. The interplay of factors with regards to their existence, causality and attributable weight-age needs to be understood in the context of management of an individual patient as well as strategic planning for control and prevention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
